  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity Building of local actors for Multi-level Agroecological Monitoring and Advocacy in Support of a Just Climate Transition</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project, led by Enda Pronat with the DyTAES (Dynamics for an Agroecological Transition in Senegal) coalition, aims to strengthen the advocacy capacity of local and national actors to promote agroecology as a response to climate change. Since 2019, DyTAES has brought together more than 80 organizations (farmers, NGOs, researchers, elected officials, and private sector). At the territorial level, it operates through DyTAEL local platforms, which test and implement agroecological practices on the ground. The project includes targeted trainings, knowledge-sharing workshops, and the development of advocacy tools (policy briefs, position papers, videos). It will also support lobbying efforts, particularly during the 2026 National Agroecology Days, to influence public policies. Through these activities, about 150 direct beneficiaries will be trained, while hundreds more will benefit indirectly, contributing to a just and sustainable climate transition in Senegal.</narrative>
  </description>
